Afro-China is the small, isolated island where the film made by the [[Org/Bisney and Dixar/Arcane Intelligence|arcane intelligence]] opens. The spire of Notre Dame rises over it, with a temple to Zeus at its top, and its people keep the Day of Destiny, when the temple's giant mandrill statue chooses the heroes who will save the world. That day it chose three villains, [[People/Hades|Hades]], [[People/Fulton|Fulton]] and [[People/Runway Brian|Runway Brian]], and set them to recover the enchanted mirror the demigod Maui had stolen. Magic on the island stops anyone from teleporting away, and past its shore the world is left unrendered, a blur of color.
